      "message": "The devicetree entry `tcpc_port0-\u003eirq_gpios` has this signal configured as active low.  However the shared TCPC interrupt code doesn\u0027t configure the pin, only named-gpios.  The corresponding [entry](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/generated.dtsi;l\u003d225) lacks the GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW flag.\n\nThe generated.dtsi file is auto-generated.  You need to do an override in [rex.dtsi](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/rex.dtsi;l\u003d14)\n\n```\nnamed-gpios {\n    /delete-node/ usb_c0_tcpc_int_odl;\n\t\tgpio_usb_c0_tcpc_int_odl: usb_c0_tcpc_int_odl {\n\t\t\tgpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpioe 0 GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW\u003e;\n\t\t\tenum-name \u003d \"GPIO_USB_C0_TCPC_INT_ODL\";\n\t\t};\n```\n\nAdd a comment noting that the util/pinmap utility doesn\u0027t support setting the active high/active low flag, so override the setting here.",
